                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7521e0ba-c248-3f81-b495-d83ca380c842",
                        "entry_id": "92167580-7ed2-38a7-b458-33c07b1727d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Obsolete spelling of lay."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "328c7922-8029-49bb-9438-870b954d9c6e",
                                "sense_id": "7521e0ba-c248-3f81-b495-d83ca380c842",
                                "text": "Ye must first remember to laye the ground, that I tould you before: which is, that it is no power inherent in the circles, or in the holines of the names of God blasphemouslie vsed: nor in whatsoeuer rites or ceremonies at that time vsed, that either can raise any infernall spirit, or yet limitat him perforce within or without these circles."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "365c4273-cf57-485b-8dd9-a79065ca0948",
                                "sense_id": "7521e0ba-c248-3f81-b495-d83ca380c842",
                                "text": "He was a wight of grisly fronte, And muckle berd ther was upon 't, His lockes farre down did laye: Ful wel he setten on his hors, Thatte fony felaws called Mors, For len it was and grai."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c1d392cf-aeb1-493d-b78b-ea103444b929",
                                "sense_id": "7521e0ba-c248-3f81-b495-d83ca380c842",
                                "text": "Aftir that, my seid lord retournyng to the campe, wold in nowise bee lodged in the same, but where he laye the furst nyght."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
